    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d521">

                <pb facs="0646" n="636" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg636"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/12–948: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi><anchor
                        n="6" xml:id="d521-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-12-09T12:00:00+08:00">December 9,
                            1948—noon.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 9—7:29 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2475. ReEmbtel 2273, to Department; 85 to Moscow, November 21, 2 p. m. Vice
                    Minister Foreign Affairs has informed Embassy officer that Foreign Office is
                    being compelled much against its will to present case of China before UN.<anchor
                        n="7" xml:id="d521-f2"/> This pressure is coming from Legislative Yuan in
                    which majority sentiment favors action and which is highly critical of Foreign
                    Office policy of appeasing Soviets at this time. Foreign Office reluctance
                    arises from what it believes would be serious loss of face to China and fear of
                    consequences arising from official and international injection of Soviets into
                    Chinese Communist problem. Vice Minister says it is highly possible Legislative
                    Yuan will attach new policy toward Soviets as a condition to vote of confidence
                    in any new Executive Yuan.</p>
                <p>Sent Department, repeated Moscow 87.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d521-f1" n="6" type="source" xml:id="d521-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to the Ambassador in France as telegram No. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Gadel</hi> 737, December 10.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d521-f2" n="7" xml:id="d521-f2-content">
                <p>United Nations.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
